      "summary": "Bruges: The Timeless Essence - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 1",
      "content": "### Chapter 3: Bruges: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Bruges - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/bruges-character.jpg)\n\nBruges feels suspended in the late Middle Ages, when it stood as northern Europe's most prosperous trading hub. Along the Rozenhoedkaai, weeping willows dip their branches into still canals that mirror picturesque stepped gables and the towering silhouette of the Belfort. White swans glide serenely along the Minnewater, the Lake of Love, framed by centuries-old ramparts and quiet weeping beech trees.\n\n![Geographic location of Bruges in Belgium](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/bruges-map.png)\n\nWhen trade silted up the Zwin river inlet in the fifteenth century, economic life slowed down, freezing Bruges in time and sparing its medieval fabric from modern industrial demolition. Today, the cobblestone Markt square echoes with horse-drawn carriage hooves. The quiet Beguinage, founded in 1245, offers whitewashed cottage facades surrounded by green lawns under ancient poplars. In the cool interiors of the Church of Our Lady, Michelangelo's serene white marble Madonna and Child watches over five hundred years of devotional silence."
