      "title": "Budapest: The Timeless Essence",
      "summary": "Budapest: The Timeless Essence - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 1",
      "content": "### Chapter 14: Budapest: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Budapest - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/budapest-character.jpg)\n\nBudapest is a dramatic tale of two cities: historic, hilly Buda with its castle and cobblestone ramparts, and vibrant, flat Pest with its wide boulevards and monumental institutions. The two halves are linked across the broad Danube River by iconic bridges, most famously the stone-towered Chain Bridge guarded by magnificent sculpted lions.\n\n![Geographic location of Budapest in Hungary](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/budapest-map.png)\n\nAlong the Pest riverbank stands the Hungarian Parliament Building, a colossal neo-Gothic masterpiece with hundreds of spires, arches, and a central dome mirrored spectacularly in the river currents at night. On the heights of Buda, the Fisherman's Bastion offers fairy-tale white towers and panoramic views over the city. Fed by over a hundred natural thermal springs, historic bathhouses like the neo-baroque Széchenyi Baths offer steaming outdoor pools where locals play chess in mineral waters under open skies."
