      "title": "Lisbon: The Timeless Essence",
      "summary": "Lisbon: The Timeless Essence - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 1",
      "content": "### Chapter 19: Lisbon: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Lisbon - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/lisbon-character.jpg)\n\nLisbon cascades over steep southern hills that open grandly toward the wide estuary of the Tagus River. Historic yellow vintage trams rattle and screech up impossibly steep cobblestone grades, most famously Tram 28 through the medieval Alfama quarter. Many historic facades are clad in glazed ceramic azulejo tiles, shimmering in brilliant blues, yellows, and greens that reflect the extraordinary clarity of the Atlantic light.\n\n![Geographic location of Lisbon in Portugal](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/lisbon-map.png)\n\nHigh above the river, the ramparts of Castelo de São Jorge offer sweeping panoramic viewpoints called miradouros, where locals and visitors gather under jacaranda trees to watch boats cross the sparkling water. Down in the waterfront district of Belém, the delicate Manueline stone carving of the Jerónimos Monastery and the Belém Tower celebrate Portugal's Age of Discovery. At night, the haunting, melancholic melodies of Fado songs echo through tiny stone taverns, singing of love, sea, and destiny."
