      "content": "### Chapter 23: Jerusalem: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Jerusalem - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/jerusalem-character.jpg)\n\nJerusalem sits atop the Judean Mountains, a city whose stone walls have witnessed three thousand years of spiritual longing, conflict, and devotion. Encircling the Old City are the massive sixteenth-century stone ramparts built by Suleiman the Magnificent. At sundown, the local dolomitic limestone—known as Jerusalem stone—absorbs the golden light and seems to glow from within.\n\n![Geographic location of Jerusalem in Israel](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/jerusalem-map.png)\n\nWithin one square kilometer, the Old City is divided into four living quarters: Jewish, Christian, Muslim, and Armenian. The Western Wall echoes with continuous prayers, while nearby the golden Dome of the Rock glitters beneath the sun upon the Temple Mount platform, and the Church of the Holy Sepulchre shelters ancient devotional chapels. In the narrow, covered bazaars, the scent of burning frankincense and ground za'atar mingles with the chimes of church bells and the melodic call to prayer."
