      "content": "### Chapter 24: Varanasi: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Varanasi - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/varanasi-character.jpg)\n\nKnown anciently as Kashi—the City of Light—Varanasi has stood along the crescent bend of the sacred Ganges River for nearly three millennia. Rising from the water's edge are eighty-four monumental stone ghats: grand flights of steps where pilgrims gather at dawn to greet the rising sun, submerge themselves in holy waters, and offer prayers to the ancestors.\n\n![Geographic location of Varanasi in India](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/varanasi-map.png)\n\nA boat ride along the river at sunrise reveals an unforgettable tableau of humanity. Golden temple spires and Rajput palazzi tower above the riverbanks, their pink and ochre facades caught in early morning mist. In the evening, the air fills with the clanging of brass bells, the blowing of conch shells, and the smoke of camphor as priests perform the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti ceremony, while thousands of small clay lamps filled with marigolds float down the darkened river."
