      "content": "### Chapter 26: Fez: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Fez - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/fez-character.jpg)\n\nFez el-Bali, the ancient walled medina of Fez founded in the eighth century, is a preserved medieval universe. Within its massive stone ramparts lie over nine thousand winding alleys and cul-de-sacs, completely free of motorized vehicles. Donkeys laden with mint, spices, and pottery navigate the narrow stone passages as artisans hammer copper pots, weave silk fabrics, and carve intricate cedarwood screens.\n\n![Geographic location of Fez in Morocco](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/fez-map.png)\n\nFrom surrounding rooftops, the sight of the famous Chouara Tannery reveals a honeycomb of round stone vats filled with colorful natural dyes—saffron yellow, poppy red, and indigo blue—where tanners work leather using techniques unchanged for a thousand years. Hidden behind plain earthen walls are breathtaking architectural treasures like the Bou Inania Madrasah, filled with exquisite carved stucco, zellige mosaic tilework, and tranquil marble fountains."
