      "content": "### Chapter 27: Cusco: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Cusco - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/cusco-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in a high Andean valley over eleven thousand feet above sea level, Cusco was revered by the Incas as the 'navel of the world.' What makes Cusco visually unique is the seamless fusion of two civilizations: Spanish colonial churches, red-tiled roofs, and carved cedar balconies built directly atop the earthquake-resistant stone foundations laid by Inca stonemasons.\n\n![Geographic location of Cusco in Peru](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/cusco-map.png)\n\nIn narrow streets like Hatun Rumiyoc, visitors marvel at the famous Twelve-Angled Stone, where enormous granite blocks fit together so precisely without mortar that a blade of grass cannot pass between them. The vast Plaza de Armas is anchored by the ornate Renaissance Cathedral of Santo Domingo, built over the palace of the Inca emperor Viracocha. Surrounding the city, terraced green mountains rise into thin mountain air, watched over by the colossal stone fortress of Sacsayhuamán."
