      "content": "### Chapter 28: Oaxaca: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Oaxaca - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/oaxaca-character.jpg)\n\nOaxaca is a vibrant colonial masterpiece constructed largely from cantera verde—a distinctive pale green volcanic stone that gives the city's historic churches and mansions an organic, earthy elegance. The Church of Santo Domingo de Guzmán stands as the pinnacle of Mexican baroque architecture, its interior covered in an astonishing cascade of gilded plasterwork, cherubs, and intricate biblical relief carvings.\n\n![Geographic location of Oaxaca in Mexico](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/oaxaca-map.png)\n\nLife centers around the shaded Zócalo, where towering laurel trees shade brass bands playing traditional marimba music while street vendors offer woven textiles, ceramic crafts, and spiced hot chocolate. Oaxaca is widely celebrated as Mexico's culinary capital, famed for its complex mole sauces, tlayudas, and artisanal mezcal. A short distance away on a flattened mountain ridge lies Monte Albán, the monumental pre-Columbian ceremonial center of the ancient Zapotec civilization."
