      "content": "### Chapter 35: Bergen: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Bergen - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/bergen-character.jpg)\n\nBergen is Norway's historic coastal capital, nestled between seven forested mountains along the shores of Byfjorden. The heart of the city's identity is Bryggen, a row of medieval wooden merchant buildings with colorful pitched gables lining the harbor, originally built by German merchants of the Hanseatic League who dominated the northern stockfish trade for centuries.\n\n![Geographic location of Bergen in Norway](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/bergen-map.png)\n\nBehind the colorful wooden facades, narrow wooden boardwalks and timber passages reveal artisan workshops, galleries, and the unmistakable scent of maritime pine tar. The Fløibanen funicular railway climbs steeply up Mount Fløyen in six minutes, opening up panoramic views over the harbor, islands, and distant fjord mouths. Surrounded by wild coastal nature, Bergen is a welcoming gateway where maritime heritage and northern wilderness meet."
