      "content": "### Chapter 36: Cartagena: The Timeless Essence\n\n![Cartagena - Iconic cityscape](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/cartagena-character.jpg)\n\nFounded in 1533 on the northern coast of South America, Cartagena de Indias served as Spain's primary maritime vault for storing the gold, silver, and emeralds harvested across the continent. To protect these treasures from pirate sieges, Spain constructed eleven kilometers of colossal stone ramparts, sea bastions, and the massive hilltop fortress of San Felipe de Barajas.\n\n![Geographic location of Cartagena in Colombia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-01/images/cartagena-map.png)\n\nWithin the fortified historic center, cobblestone streets are lined with brilliantly painted colonial houses in shades of saffron, cobalt, coral, and sunshine yellow. Wooden balconies overflow with vibrant fuchsia bougainvillea, while heavy carved wooden doorways feature brass knockers shaped like sea creatures and lions. As the tropical evening brings cool sea breezes, horse-drawn carriages clatter across plazas where music, street dancers, and laughter celebrate Caribbean life."
